{"id":"kodak_exr_100t","name":"Kodak EXR 100T","manufacturer":"Kodak","kind":"Cine negative","isBlackAndWhite":false,"source":"Negs","targetPrint":"kodak_2383","datasheet":{"url":"https://125px.com/docs/motionpicture/kodak/5248.pdf","title":"Eastman EXR 100T 5248/7248, H-1-7248 (1999)"},"credit":"Copyright (c) 2026 Noah Haasis (Negs preparation). Method and generic dye spectra by Andrea Volpato (spektrafilm). Measurement data (c) Eastman Kodak Company.","license":"Negs film profile, licensed under CC BY-SA 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/). Prepared with the profile-creation method of spektrafilm by Andrea Volpato (https://github.com/andreavolpato/spektrafilm; profiles CC BY-SA 4.0, see SPEKTRAFILM_LICENSE.txt) and its generic dye spectra. Derivatives must credit both, note their modifications and remain CC BY-SA 4.0. Changes: data/CHANGELOG.txt.","dataSource":"Prepared for Negs from the manufacturer's datasheet: EASTMAN EXR 100T Color Negative Film 5248/7248, Technical Data / Color Negative Film, KODAK Publication No. H-1-7248, March 1999 (©Eastman Kodak Company, 1999; Minor Revision 3-99), PDF page 3 (spectral sensitivity, characteristic curves, minimum and midscale-neutral spectral density; RMS granularity less than 5). PDF sha256 4735518c66d406e508928715f932a626b9f1e23647d45fd84f8c3cd4133291fc. Data (c) Eastman Kodak Company. The curves were read from the PDF's vector paths (tools/film_profiles/extract_pdf.py); the points and axis calibration are in data/profile-sources/kodak-cine/kodak_exr_100t/.\nMethod: spektrafilm's public-era profile creator by Andrea Volpato (commit b2c7fe6), steps 1-8: D-min removed, log E zero where green is 0.2 over D-min plus 3 stops, dye spectra reconstructed (dmid_dmin) from spektrafilm's generic_a dye set (Giorgianni, Madden & Kriss 2009, p. 112, via spektrafilm) because the datasheet gives no per-dye spectra, status-M unmixing, a 3 norm_cdfs curve fit, sensitivity balance, midscale alignment 'mid' (of none/green/mid, the lowest grey-ramp neutrality error, none 0.085, green 0.058, mid 0.049, among those whose kodak_2383 neutral filters fall in the shipped films' range), densitometer normalisation. Then Negs's steps: sensitivity scaled so an 18.4 % grey gives raw exposure 1 per channel under the reference illuminant, and spektrafilm's grey-ramp refinement run on spektrafilm 28bf883 through kodak_2383 at data_trustability 0.3. hanatos2025 adaptation window [394.4, 21.5, 610.4, 59.2] fitted on the reflectance corpus (Otsu (https://github.com/enneract/otsu2018), Munsell (https://zenodo.org/records/3269912), human skin (https://www.nist.gov/programs-projects/reflectance-measurements-human-skin), forest colors (https://zenodo.org/records/3269920)) with a weak prior toward the median of spektrafilm's stored windows. Tools and procedure: tools/film_profiles, docs/adding-film-stocks.md.\nNegs choices: reference illuminant T, colour-science's incandescent SPD, as Kodak's tungsten Vision3 profiles (tungsten stock, exposed at 3200 K); viewing illuminant D50; target print kodak_2383; log_sensitivity_density_over_min 0.4 as printed; spectra left empty (null) outside the published wavelength range; characteristic curves in log10 H as printed (the chart's log lux-seconds scale); use 'cine' and antihalation 'strong' as the Vision3 and Eterna profiles.\nWindow prior weight 0.003 instead of 0.002: at the default 0.002 the fit put c_uv at 389.1 nm, under the shipped windows' range (391-456; D8 check 10); 0.003 is the smallest of 0.003/0.004/0.006/0.01 that passes, giving [394.4, 21.5, 610.4, 59.2] at a corpus loss 2 % above the unconstrained fit (0.0215 against 0.0211; no window 0.0276).\nNote: The characteristic chart has two exposure scales: log lux-seconds on top (ticks 3-bar.0 to 1.0, labelled at both frame edges) and camera stops below. They disagree by 9 % (one drawn stop is 0.276 log10 H on the top scale, not 0.301). The curves are read on the top scale, the sensitometric one, which gives a green mid-scale gamma of about 0.59; the stop scale would give about 0.54.","referenceIlluminant":"T","densitometer":"status_M","densityMinimum":[0.181,0.569,0.962],"wavelengths":[380,385,390,395,400,405,410,415,420,425,430,435,440,445,450,455,460,465,470,475,480,485,490,495,500,505,510,515,520,525,530,535,540,545,550,555,560,565,570,575,580,585,590,595,600,605,610,615,620,625,630,635,640,645,650,655,660,665,670,675,680,685,690,695,700,705,710,715,720,725,730,735,740,745,750,755,760,765,770,775,780],"logSensitivity":[[null,null,null],[null,null,null],[null,null,null],[null,null,null],[null,-1.5756,-0.45953],[null,-1.5476,-0.36828],[null,-1.5539,-0.33268],[null,-1.6091,-0.34303],[-2.4358,-1.6984,-0.36477],[-2.4789,-1.7624,-0.34782],[-2.5794,-1.7975,-0.29529],[-2.6828,-1.8095,-0.24075],[-2.746,-1.8104,-0.19168],[-2.7635,-1.8116,-0.14343],[-2.7718,-1.8004,-0.086313],[-2.8022,-1.7658,-0.011068],[-2.8842,-1.7506,0.089076],[-3.0322,-1.7878,0.21474],[-3.1348,-1.8167,0.28863],[-3.0656,-1.7231,0.23952],[-2.9551,-1.522,0.075086],[-2.8873,-1.3678,-0.22383],[-2.8433,-1.2613,-0.65144],[-2.8055,-1.1836,-1.091],[-2.7561,-1.11,-1.4916],[-2.6688,-1.0153,-1.8237],[-2.562,-0.9002,-2.0829],[-2.4772,-0.78232,-2.3025],[-2.4133,-0.65917,-2.5089],[-2.3677,-0.52779,null],[-2.3394,-0.41326,null],[-2.3239,-0.32715,null],[-2.3029,-0.25071,null],[-2.2577,-0.17589,null],[-2.1822,-0.1337,null],[-2.0654,-0.14788,null],[-1.9028,-0.21322,null],[-1.716,-0.33371,null],[-1.5189,-0.5759,null],[-1.3209,-1.109,null],[-1.1626,-1.6467,null],[-1.0579,-2.0117,null],[-0.97922,-2.3093,null],[-0.90428,-2.582,null],[-0.82712,null,null],[-0.75374,null,null],[-0.71839,null,null],[-0.73616,null,null],[-0.75655,null,null],[-0.7249,null,null],[-0.64623,null,null],[-0.55911,null,null],[-0.50187,null,null],[-0.48373,null,null],[-0.50423,null,null],[-0.58256,null,null],[-0.75141,null,null],[-1.0169,null,null],[-1.3574,null,null],[-1.7348,null,null],[-2.1022,null,null],[-2.4362,null,null],[null,null,null],[null,null,